          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Criticisms and Controversy</strong><br>\nDespite his acclaim, Greenspan's policies have also been criticized. Some blame his approach to deregulation and his belief in self-regulating markets for contributing to the financial crises of 2001 and 2008. He admitted in 2008 that he had put too much faith in the self-correcting power of free markets.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Continuing Influence</strong><br>\nAfter retiring from the Federal Reserve in 2006, Greenspan formed Greenspan Associates LLC, a consulting firm. He has written several books sharing his experience and views on economic policy. Even in retirement, his opinions on economic matters are highly sought after, and he remains a respected figure in the field of economics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Greenspan's Legacy</strong><br>\nAlan Greenspan's legacy in the world of economics is complex. He is often praised for his leadership during a period of remarkable growth in the United States. However, his legacy is also marred by the role his policies may have played in economic downturns. Still, his influence on economic policy and his reputation as a skilled economist endure.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
